From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:58:04 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Windows 10 Mobile: 96 MB, not 512, set aside for array
 buffers

One process is the browser, the GPU thread and every renderer there, in
2 GB of address space. The half gigabyte Blink reserves on 32-bit Windows
is taken from Direct3D's textures and swap chains, DLLs and thread stacks,
none of which can ask for it back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../blink/renderer/controller/blink_initializer.cc  | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/controller/blink_initializer.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/controller/blink_initializer.cc
index 4d1f2acf58e43bf8d5e19294133647387f03cd0a..8ba2bd6fc4ba3b4938a0022762b7cf56226f0b7b 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/controller/blink_initializer.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/controller/blink_initializer.cc
@@ -131,7 +131,18 @@ void InitializeCommon(Platform* platform, mojo::BinderMap* binders) {
   if (!is_wow_64) {
     // Try to reserve as much address space as we reasonably can.
     const size_t kMB = 1024 * 1024;
-    for (size_t size = 512 * kMB; size >= 32 * kMB; size -= 16 * kMB) {
+#if defined(VENETIUM_W10M)
+    // One process is the browser, the GPU thread and every renderer here, in
+    // 2 GB of address space. Half a gigabyte set aside for array buffers is
+    // taken from Direct3D's textures and swap chains, from DLLs and thread
+    // stacks, none of which can ask for it back. A piece small enough to
+    // spare is kept as PartitionAlloc's last resort.
+    const size_t kLargestReservation = 96 * kMB;
+#else
+    const size_t kLargestReservation = 512 * kMB;
+#endif
+    for (size_t size = kLargestReservation; size >= 32 * kMB;
+         size -= 16 * kMB) {
       if (partition_alloc::ReserveAddressSpace(size)) {
         break;
       }
